        "timestamp": 1781085021,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran targets US bases in Jordan and the Gulf after Trump orders strikes near Hormuz Issued on: 10/06/2026 - 11:50 Iran's Revolutionary Guards ​said they had carried out missile and drone attacks on U.S. military bases in Jordan, Kuwait and Bahrain on Wednesday in retaliation for American strikes on Iranian targets around the Strait of Hormuz. The clashes mark one of the biggest exchanges in hostilities since the two countries agreed to a ceasefire in April and came after U.S. President Donald Trump said Iran had downed a U.S. Apache helicopter near the strait on Tuesday. 09/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Trump vows response after Iran shoots down US helicopter 09/06/2026 Middle East Trump immigration stance 'clashes against reality of what is needed to stage a truly global event' 09/06/2026 Americas FCAS project failure: 'France, Germany characterised by totally different strategic cultures' 09/06/2026 Europe Lebanon says 8 dead in strike on Tyre as Israel keeps up attacks on south 09/06/2026 Middle East France bans Israeli minister Smotrich in coordinated sanctions push 09/06/2026 Middle East France: Lyhanna's death reveals 'entire system is broken' 09/06/2026 Bear captured in Japan after multi-day search as attacks rise 09/06/2026 Asia / Pacific 2026 World Cup participation conditional to US travel restrictions 09/06/2026 Americas"
